": "heading", "content": " Present Simple vs. Present Continuous "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present tense</span> to talk about: <ul><li>routine actions that don't change</li><li> things that are always true</li></ul>You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous tense</span>  to talk about:<ul><li>actions that are happening right now</li><li>future plans</li></ul>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Present Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Continuous Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Routines: <br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I post about Paris on my blog.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Right now: <br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I am walking through the streets of Paris.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Always true: <br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Paris is a beautiful city.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future plans: <br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm posting a new entry on my blog about my adventure later! </span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dream"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that is beautiful, excellent or pleasing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Paris is a dream!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when writing a letter about a place in a city."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wish you were here"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "use this to say you miss someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I wish you were here in Paris with me!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "menu board "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a board on which you write a food menu"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  People write on the menu board."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "along"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in a line"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(preposition)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The menu boards are along the sidewalk."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sidewalk"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a concrete path along the side of a street for people to walk on"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Walk on the sidewalk, not on the road."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "a little bit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small amount"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can see a little bit of Paris."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to light up "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to fill up; illuminate"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Eiffel Tower lights up the sky at night."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob02aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sky"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the space where the sun and moon appear"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It lights up the entire sky."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob02aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "entry"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that is posted on a blog"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm a posting a new entry on my blog."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob02aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "adventure "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an exciting experience"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am enjoying this adventure!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob02aud10"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le01ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go on the internet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen to the song, \"Wish You Were Here\" by Pink Floyd. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find the lyrics to this song. Print them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Circle all the verbs in the Simple Present tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change those verbs into the Present Continuous tense."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I circle the verbs in the Simple Present tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use the Present Continuous tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I review lyrics from a song from the internet."}]}], "type": "sena"}